<title>ITALY: Italy's Pirelli plans share buyback.</title>
<headline>Italy's Pirelli plans share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian tyre and cablemaker Pirelli said in a statement it planned to make a share buyback of up to 300 billion lire within 18 months.</p>
<p>Pirelli, which earlier announced it intended to offer an ordinary dividend of 100 lire per share against 50 lire previously, also said it saw positive prospects for 1997.</p>
<p>It intended to schedule its annual shareholder meeting for May 12 or 13, it said.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
